WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:18.117
Jonathan and his parents got to the field early on Saturday afternoon for the game.

2
00:00:19.077 --> 00:00:22.039
His dad set up their chairs near Carlos' mom and some other parents.

3
00:00:25.261 --> 00:00:27.162
Jonathan spotted Marissa on the sideline.

4
00:00:27.862 --> 00:00:30.564
She wore a cute yellow sundress and a turquoise straw hat.

5
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:34.189
Marissa glanced at Jonathan, frowned, and turned away.

6
00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:37.070
Jonathan took a deep breath and walked over to her.

7
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:40.971
Marissa scowled.

8
00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:42.311
"What do you want?"

9
00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:44.572
Jonathan took a very deep breath.

10
00:00:44.592 --> 00:00:46.512
"I want to apologize.

11
00:00:47.212 --> 00:00:51.974
I mean, I don't want to apologize, because it's really difficult for me because I'm so nervous.

12
00:00:52.954 --> 00:00:55.835
But also, I do want to apologize because you deserve it.

13
00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:57.435
An apology, I mean."

14
00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:00.896
Marissa raised her eyebrows at him as he babbled on.

15
00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.809
At least she'd stopped scowling.

16
00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.650
"I shouldn't have mad-mouthed your family.

17
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.651
I mean, bad-mouthed your family," Jonathan said.

18
00:01:08.671 --> 00:01:10.772
"I didn't know that was your family.

19
00:01:11.512 --> 00:01:12.213
But now I know.

20
00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.934
I mean, I realized it right after I said it.

21
00:01:15.974 --> 00:01:18.655
I mean Jonathan took another deep breath.

22
00:01:18.675 --> 00:01:21.817
"I'm really sorry."

23
00:01:22.817 --> 00:01:24.178
Marissa looked slightly amused.

24
00:01:25.278 --> 00:01:27.859
"That was the longest, most confusing apology I've ever heard."

25
00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.480
"I'm sorry for that."

26
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.061
"Now you're apologizing for your apology?"

27
00:01:32.401 --> 00:01:33.201
Marissa smiled.

28
00:01:33.221 --> 00:01:35.302
"It's okay, Jonathan.

29
00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.442
I understand what you were trying to say.

30
00:01:38.102 --> 00:01:38.843
And I forgive you."

31
00:01:39.823 --> 00:01:41.103
Jonathan took another deep breath.

32
00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:45.404
This one was a big sigh of relief.

33
00:01:45.424 --> 00:01:50.166
"I mean, I didn't like hearing you insult my brother and father," Marissa went on.

34
00:01:50.186 --> 00:01:52.867
"But I understand why people get frustrated with them.

35
00:01:53.807 --> 00:01:57.528
Dad gets carried away by Max's soccer skills, and he forgets about the rest of the team.

36
00:01:58.812 --> 00:02:00.312
And Max just goes along with Dad."

37
00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:02.113
Jonathan nodded.

38
00:02:02.933 --> 00:02:04.594
Then he tried to think of something nice to say.

39
00:02:04.614 --> 00:02:09.275
"Max is really talented, and your father seems to know a lot about soccer."

40
00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.476
"True," she said.

41
00:02:11.496 --> 00:02:13.676
"But Dad needs to learn how to chill out."

42
00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:15.757
"Team meeting!"

43
00:02:16.397 --> 00:02:17.877
Coach Wattenbarger yelled just then.

44
00:02:17.897 --> 00:02:19.798
"Boys, get over here!

45
00:02:20.058 --> 00:02:22.799
Now!" "I have to go," Jonathan said.

46
00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:25.860
"Let's talk again soon," Marissa said.

47
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:31.338
"Okay!" Jonathan wanted to act cool, but a huge grin took over his whole face.

48
00:02:32.799 --> 00:02:35.121
He got to the meeting just as his coach started talking.

49
00:02:35.141 --> 00:02:39.824
"We're playing the Spitting Cobras today," the coach said.

50
00:02:39.844 --> 00:02:42.146
"They won their first two games.

51
00:02:42.766 --> 00:02:45.848
But we can beat them if everyone keeps passing the ball to Max."

52
00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:47.990
Jonathan started to protest.

53
00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.091
"Coach—" "Dad.

54
00:02:50.672 --> 00:02:52.753
I'm too sick to play today," Max said.

55
00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.434
He clutched his stomach.

56
00:02:56.155 --> 00:02:56.956
The coach frowned.

57
00:02:57.628 --> 00:03:00.210
"You told me your stomach hurt, but you didn't want to go to the doctor."

58
00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:04.232
"My stomach doesn't hurt enough for a doctor visit," Max said.

59
00:03:04.252 --> 00:03:07.954
"Then it doesn't hurt enough to skip the game," the coach snapped.

60
00:03:07.974 --> 00:03:10.696
"You'll get in there and play, like a pro!"

61
00:03:10.716 --> 00:03:13.197
"Poor Max," Jonathan thought.

62
00:03:13.217 --> 00:03:17.299
"I also think I'm coming down with a bad cold."

63
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:24.483
Max sneezed loudly, and Carlos caught Jonathan's eye as if they were both thinking the same thing—was that

64
00:03:24.523 --> 00:03:25.384
a fake sneeze?

65
00:03:26.588 --> 00:03:30.430
"Max, we can't win without you," Coach Wattenbarger was saying.

66
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.732
"You're the backbone of this team!"

67
00:03:32.752 --> 00:03:36.714
"No, I'm not," Max replied in a shaky voice.

68
00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.755
"And you can win without me.

69
00:03:39.515 --> 00:03:40.696
Jonathan is really good.

70
00:03:41.536 --> 00:03:42.657
He can play forward today."

71
00:03:43.577 --> 00:03:44.518
Jonathan shook his head.

72
00:03:44.538 --> 00:03:46.719
"I'm not nearly as good as you, Max."

73
00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:52.282
"Max, you're the best player in the league," his father said for the millionth time that season.

74
00:03:52.302 --> 00:03:55.084
"I'm the sickest player in the league today."

75
00:03:55.752 --> 00:03:56.933
Max bent over and coughed.

76
00:03:59.154 --> 00:04:00.374
Coach Wattenbarger sighed.

77
00:04:00.394 --> 00:04:02.175
"All right, Max.

78
00:04:02.795 --> 00:04:03.715
Rest on the sideline.

79
00:04:04.416 --> 00:04:05.736
Jonathan, play forward."

80
00:04:06.977 --> 00:04:09.898
Jonathan had been dying to play forward since the soccer season had started.

81
00:04:10.678 --> 00:04:13.300
But he didn't want to do it now, not without Max.

82
00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.121
He hurried toward Max and took him aside.

83
00:04:16.141 --> 00:04:22.563
"You may be the best soccer player in the league, but you're the worst actor in the world,"

84
00:04:22.924 --> 00:04:23.464
he whispered.

85
00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.741
"Stop pretending to be sick.

86
00:04:26.521 --> 00:04:27.422
Our team needs you.

87
00:04:28.123 --> 00:04:31.625
And we want you to play—as long as the rest of us can play with you!"

88
00:04:32.686 --> 00:04:33.466
Max shook his head.

89
00:04:33.486 --> 00:04:35.988
"Come on, Max," Jonathan said.

90
00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.089
"Everyone get on the field.

91
00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:39.830
The game's about to start!"

92
00:04:40.391 --> 00:04:41.452
Coach Wattenbarger yelled.

93
00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:43.293
Max didn't move.

94
00:04:43.313 --> 00:04:45.454
"Just go, Jonathan!"

95
00:04:46.895 --> 00:04:49.057
Jonathan glared at him before running onto the field.

96
00:04:51.298 --> 00:04:53.600
He and his teammates lined up against the Spitting Cobras.

97
00:04:54.676 --> 00:04:56.838
He hoped the Spitting Cobras didn't actually spit!

98
00:04:57.578 --> 00:05:00.600
The Cobras had two substitutes and were big and fierce-looking.

99
00:05:01.561 --> 00:05:05.203
Meanwhile, because of Max's "illness," the Wattenbargers were missing a player.

100
00:05:06.244 --> 00:05:10.187
Facing the Cobras, the Wattenbargers appeared small and timid to Jonathan.

101
00:05:11.107 --> 00:05:12.568
The Spitting Cobras started strong.

102
00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:15.050
They passed the ball up the field, near the goal.

103
00:05:15.831 --> 00:05:17.131
One of their forwards took a shot.

104
00:05:21.134 --> 00:05:27.037
Luckily, a Wattenbarger defender blocked the ball, kicking it to a Wattenbarger midfielder, who kicked it to Jonathan.

105
00:05:28.138 --> 00:05:31.219
Here, finally, was Jonathan's chance to score!

106
00:05:35.041 --> 00:05:37.102
But a huge Spitting Cobra moved in front of him.

107
00:05:37.862 --> 00:05:40.724
Jonathan looked around but couldn't find anyone open for a pass.

108
00:05:43.705 --> 00:05:45.846
He didn't like the pressure of being the only forward.

109
00:05:46.506 --> 00:05:49.828
He tried to dribble the ball, but the huge Cobra in front of him forced him out of

110
00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:55.744
bounds. The huge Cobra took the throw-in.

111
00:05:56.465 --> 00:05:59.946
He threw the ball far up the field to his teammate, who kicked it to another teammate.

112
00:06:04.027 --> 00:06:07.468
That guy kicked it just out of reach of the Wattenbarger goalie and into the goal.

113
00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:12.449
Jonathan looked at Max in dismay.

114
00:06:13.089 --> 00:06:15.950
But on the sideline, Max just stared down at the ground.

115
00:06:17.451 --> 00:06:23.012
The Spitting Cobras didn't score any more goals in the first half, but neither did the Wattenbargers.

116
00:06:23.032 --> 00:06:26.733
Jonathan was grateful that he got to play his hardest instead of just giving Max the ball as

117
00:06:26.773 --> 00:06:27.953
he'd done the first two games.

118
00:06:28.974 --> 00:06:31.174
But it didn't feel right for Max to be on the sideline.

119
00:06:31.854 --> 00:06:33.755
Plus, he wouldn't mind scoring a goal.

120
00:06:34.855 --> 00:06:39.277
Once the Wattenbargers got off the field, their coach shouted, "What a terrible first half!

121
00:06:40.197 --> 00:06:41.357
Take a two-minute water break.

122
00:06:41.977 --> 00:06:43.538
Then get over here for a team meeting."

123
00:06:44.598 --> 00:06:47.459
Jonathan grabbed his water bottle and hurried to where Max was sitting.

124
00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:51.680
"We need you on the field."

125
00:06:52.872 --> 00:06:53.813
Max rubbed his stomach.

126
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:55.014
"I'm sick."

127
00:06:55.034 --> 00:07:00.958
"I think you're just sick of your dad's coaching style and too scared to tell him," Jonathan said.

128
00:07:00.978 --> 00:07:04.320
"Just like I was scared to apologize to you and your sister.

129
00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.062
But after I did, I felt a lot better."

130
00:07:08.202 --> 00:07:08.903
Max sighed.

131
00:07:08.923 --> 00:07:13.386
"Besides, you can't pretend to be sick all season.

132
00:07:14.487 --> 00:07:17.228
We still have a bunch of games left," Jonathan said.

133
00:07:18.109 --> 00:07:18.890
Max sighed again.

134
00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:22.312
"Okay, I'll talk to my dad.

135
00:07:22.892 --> 00:07:24.294
But he won't like what I have to say."
